<span class="h5" id="autoid-14"><a class="selflink" id="section-3.1.2.1" href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7231#section-3.1.2.1">3.1.2.1</a>.  Content Codings</span><font></font>
<font></font>
   Content coding values indicate an encoding transformation that has<font></font>
   been or can be applied to a representation.  Content codings are<font></font>
   primarily used to allow a representation to be compressed or<font></font>
   otherwise usefully transformed without losing the identity of its<font></font>
   underlying media type and without loss of information.  Frequently,<font></font>
   the representation is stored in coded form, transmitted directly, and<font></font>
   only decoded by the final recipient.<font></font>
<font></font>
     content-coding   = token<font></font>
<font></font>
   All content-coding values are case-insensitive and ought to be<font></font>
