<font></font>
   Responses to the OPTIONS method are not cacheable.<font></font>
<font></font>
<span class="h4" id="autoid-41"><a class="selflink" id="section-4.3.8" href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7231#section-4.3.8">4.3.8</a>.  TRACE</span><font></font>
<font></font>
   The TRACE method requests a remote, application-level loop-back of<font></font>
   the request message.  The final recipient of the request SHOULD<font></font>
   reflect the message received, excluding some fields described below,<font></font>
   back to the client as the message body of a 200 (OK) response with a<font></font>
   Content-Type of "message/http" (<a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7230#section-8.3.1">Section&nbsp;8.3.1 of [RFC7230]</a>).  The<font></font>
   final recipient is either the origin server or the first server to<font></font>
   receive a Max-Forwards value of zero (0) in the request<font></font>
   (<a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7231#section-5.1.2">Section 5.1.2</a>).<font></font>
